Main code compiles. Now write tests.

Test infrastructure:
- `src/test/resources/application.yaml`: H2 url with random db name, no DB_CLOSE_DELAY.
- `src/test/java/com/example/starter/MutableClock.java`
- `src/test/java/com/example/starter/TestClockConfig.java` — @TestConfiguration with @Primary MutableClock bean. But @TestConfiguration needs to be picked up; nested static class in test or standalone with @Import. I'll make a standalone @TestConfiguration class and @Import it in each test class.

Wait: main Clock bean + @Primary MutableClock → service gets MutableClock. Good.

Test classes:
1. `DirectiveApiTest` — @SpringBootTest + @AutoConfigureMockMvc, covers main flow & failure branches & idempotency & late correction & queries.
2. `DirectiveConcurrencyTest` — @SpringBootTest, uses service directly with ExecutorService.

Cleanup: @BeforeEach JdbcTemplate delete all rows (order: reconciliation_difference, reconciliation_sample, reconciliation, directive_sample, curtailment_directive). Keep power_unit seeds.

Helper methods in tests: create directive via MockMvc, confirm, report readings, reconcile.

Clock control: MutableClock bean autowired; set time per test. Base times:
